      "_tint_note": "Loupe brand pink #FFF0F9 (Charlie, 2026-07-29 — replaced the original #89b0f0 blue). tint = tile wash + the fill behind the photo; tintInk (navy) is the badge fill and the tinted-card text; tintBorder draws the frame. MEASURED CONTRAST is why tintBorder is no longer #F3CBF0: against a white card that pink is 1.44:1 and the wash itself is 1.10:1 — i.e. the partner cue was, correctly, invisible, which is exactly what Charlie reported. #C75FB6 is the SAME HUE (310° vs 306°) two steps darker and measures 3.66:1 on white / 3.50:1 on the Discover background, clearing the WCAG 1.4.11 3:1 floor for a graphic that identifies a component. The pale wash stays as specified — the frame is what does the work. All flat colours, no gradients. Data-only: edit here, re-run the refresh, and every partner tile restyles with NO app release.",
